---

<script>
	const quizResults = [
		{ week: 'Week 1', score: 76 },
		{ week: 'Week 2', score: 82 },
		{ week: 'Week 3', score: 89 }
	];

	const averageScore = Math.round(
		quizResults.reduce((sum, item) => sum + item.score, 0) / quizResults.length
	);
</script>

Creating a new post is still simple:

1. Add a new `.svx` file in `src/posts`.
2. Fill out frontmatter (`title`, `description`, `date`, optional `tags`).
3. Write markdown and embed Svelte markup as needed.

## Data-aware content block

<table>
	<thead>
		<tr>
			<th>Period</th>
			<th>Average Score</th>
		</tr>
	</thead>
	<tbody>
		{#each quizResults as result}
			<tr>
				<td>{result.week}</td>
				<td>{result.score}%</td>
			</tr>
		{/each}
	</tbody>
</table>

<p><strong>Current trend average:</strong> {averageScore}%</p>

With `.svx`, posts can evolve from static text into interactive learning experiences.
